<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zelaya Department</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Department of Zelaya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zelaya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a> was the large department of eastern Nicaragua formed from the former Mosquito Reserve after its forcible incorporation in 1894, and named after President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-santos-zelaya">José Santos Zelaya</a>. It covered the whole <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> coast, home to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miskito">Miskito</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creole</a> and other communities. In the 1980s it was divided, and in 1987 its lands became the two autonomous regions of the Caribbean coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zelaya-department.jpg" alt="Zelaya Department" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zelaya_in_Nicaragua.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
